**Definition 10.1 (full same-run recurrence).** Evaluate the exact expanded
$G_\circ$ from its actual entrance, never an old-G run plus an independently
optimized increment. Let $N_{o,p}$ count actual opcode/purpose pairs,
$A$ all constructed nonmeter cells and $b_{\rm ctl}$ all constructed
finite bits, active/inactive. Refine entering purposes by initialization,
each arrow, each decoder, each Publish/check, cleanup and original return;
a helper inherits its purpose unless its explicit CTL changes it.
Use ARC Definition 10.1's complete-successor recurrence for each leaf:

$$
\begin{aligned}
N_{o,p}'&=N_{o,p}+[(o,p)=(o_i,p_i)],\\
A'&=A+a_i,& b_{\rm ctl}'&=b_{\rm ctl}+c_i,\\
C_\tau'&=C_\tau+[o_i=\mathrm{IN}_\tau],\\
\mathrm{tick}'&=\mathrm{tick}+1,&\mathrm{fee}'&=\mathrm{fee}+2,\\
\mathrm{material}'&=\mathrm{material}+8a_i+c_i+8.
\end{aligned}
$$

Here $a_i=1$ for a core nonmeter EX/boundary cell, else zero; $c_i=1$
for a newly constructed finite bit, else zero. Sequence evaluates the
next cost at the preceding complete successor. Tests use their real
RD/CTL branches and heads; while uses the real updated bank/parity.
